WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.060
Everyone knows that voting is terrible, but have you ever wondered what makes voting such an awful thing to do?

00:05.800 --> 00:06.700
Well, I'll tell you.

00:07.560 --> 00:12.260
First, it's too expensive. On average, it costs $100 to vote in each state.

00:12.700 --> 00:13.660
That's a lot of money.

00:14.060 --> 00:16.120
And if you don't think so, then picture it like this.

00:16.420 --> 00:21.600
If you got $100 bills and placed them end-to-end, you'd have a line 100 feet long.

00:21.720 --> 00:24.600
And if you have a lot more money than that, then you have $1 million.

00:25.320 --> 00:26.860
Think about that next time you vote.

00:27.440 --> 00:28.060
A million.

00:28.060 --> 00:30.660
Second, you'll probably be working.

00:31.120 --> 00:33.500
Voting is usually held on Tuesday during work hours.

00:33.900 --> 00:37.180
Good luck convincing your employer to give you time off in the middle of the day.

00:37.500 --> 00:41.260
Third, unless you've submitted your Q-83 form, it's probably too late.

00:41.580 --> 00:43.120
It must be filled out by hand.

00:43.220 --> 00:45.780
To print it, navigate your browser to the following address.

00:45.900 --> 00:49.100
Typing it incorrectly will put your computer at risk of spam.

00:49.200 --> 00:52.800
You will then need to contact your system administrator for permission to print this document.

00:52.920 --> 00:55.480
To find your system administrator, contact this address.

00:55.480 --> 01:01.500
You will receive information via a pre-recorded message sent to the phone number associated with your name in the most recent census.

01:01.600 --> 01:04.720
Once your Q-83 form is printed, you must fill it out very carefully.

01:04.800 --> 01:07.680
Filling it out incorrectly exposes you to federal prosecution.

01:07.960 --> 01:11.920
Once completed, you must submit it in person at the Municipal Department of Registrars.

01:11.920 --> 01:14.400
It is a very large building that is very difficult to navigate.

01:14.400 --> 01:17.060
If you ask people for help, they will not know what you are talking about.

01:17.220 --> 01:19.920
It will be obvious to them that you are lost and confused.

01:20.080 --> 01:23.860
And once you leave, they will all talk about you as though you are stupid.

01:23.920 --> 01:25.640
They will all see you.

01:25.640 --> 01:29.280
That brings us to the next reason you should never vote.

01:29.720 --> 01:31.300
People will think you are strange.

01:31.900 --> 01:33.680
Look at these people lined up to vote.

01:33.800 --> 01:35.160
They're not doing anything.

01:35.340 --> 01:37.540
They're just standing around doing nothing.

01:38.140 --> 01:40.540
Everyone else thinks that they are very strange.

01:41.260 --> 01:43.640
You don't want other people to think that you're strange.

01:44.580 --> 01:46.900
Fifth, all of the candidates are bad.

01:47.680 --> 01:48.400
All of them.

01:49.380 --> 01:50.640
Especially this one.

01:50.640 --> 01:54.480
He's the very worst one.

01:56.240 --> 02:00.000
And finally, mathematically speaking, your vote doesn't count for much.

02:00.360 --> 02:03.640
Each year, 1,000 Americans cast a vote for president.

02:04.140 --> 02:05.980
Obviously, you only have one vote.

02:06.300 --> 02:09.960
So that means your vote only counts for 1% of the overall vote.

02:10.600 --> 02:12.720
Plus the electoral stuff, so who cares.

02:12.820 --> 02:15.460
And plus all of the government problems with the money debt.

02:15.680 --> 02:17.740
You think that everything in the government is so great?

02:17.980 --> 02:19.660
Well, some of it is actually bad.

02:19.660 --> 02:22.600
Plus voter fraud with all of the fraud.

02:23.000 --> 02:24.060
Think about it.
